+# The Story That Makes the Change Legible
+
+## Concept
+
+A career transition becomes a clear route across a map. The lesson begins with a gap between an established past and an emerging future, then draws a bright bridge through three story-building moves: backstory, turning point, and forward case. Three warning cards expose common narrative failures before the finished story resolves into a confident, concise path.
+
+## Visual system
+
+- Editorial map language: route lines, nodes, labels, and structured cards.
+- Navy anchors the established career; blue carries the transition; gold marks decisions and proof.
+- Every scene advances the same route rather than introducing unrelated metaphors.
+- Large, sparse typography keeps the argument readable at a glance.
+
+## Motion
+
+- A single paused GSAP timeline controls all animation and is safe to seek.
+- Route segments draw forward; cards lift into place; emphasis words resolve in gold.
+- Transitions use short opacity and position changes, with no looping motion.
+
